# End-to-end EMULATOR test for the Duet2 WiFi/Ethernet (Atmel SAM4E8E)
# in DETERMINISTIC TICK MODE. Boots klipper firmware under Renode
# against the duet2 pin map, completes klippy identify + clocksync,
# brings up the full MCU config (4 TMC2660s on USART-SPI, 2
# software-PWM heaters, a fan, endstops, 2 thermistors), reads the
# thermistors through the SAM4E AFEC, round-trips the TMC2660 register
# files over the SPI bus, and exercises interactive gcode (M114/M105).
#
# This is the SAM4E per-printer test, the SAM4E sibling of duet2_maestro
# (SAM4S) and the counterpart to sam4e_smoke (boot only). It exercises:
#
#   - The TMC2660 SPI sub-mode of the renode_hooks spidev_transfer
#     responder. TMC2660 uses 3-byte (20-bit) datagrams instead of the
#     5-byte/40-bit datagrams of tmc2130/5160/2240, so spi_tmc_chip
#     (auto-emitted per [tmc2660 ...] section) switches the responder
#     into a 3-byte path. DUMP_TMC below reads the live response register
#     for stepper_x and the extruder; a broken SPI round-trip would trip
#     "failed to init" or a read error.
#   - The SAM4E AFEC ADC, reusing test/emulator/afec_stub.py (the same
#     stub SAME70 uses - src/atsam/sam4e_afec.c is shared). The extruder
#     reads through AFEC0 channel index 7 (PC15) and the bed through
#     index 6 (PC13), both EPCOS 100K. With a broken AFEC both heaters
#     sit at temp=0.0 with no shutdown, so the "temp=3" assertion (both
#     read ~36 C) is the positive proof the AFEC delivered samples.
#
# The real Duet2 host link is USB; the firmware here is the generic
# serial-mode sam4e8e build (host link on PA9/PA10) and the test
# exercises the pin map, which is independent of the host link. The
# gated path is motion-free.
DICTIONARY sam4e8e.dict
CONFIG duet2_wifi.cfg
EMULATOR duet2_wifi.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

# Interactive gcode round-trip against real firmware in tick mode.
M114
M105
# Read back the live TMC2660 response register over the SPI bus for the
# first and last drivers.
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

# Tick-mode advances simavr only when klippy sends an advance command,
# so a tight gcode burst (M114/M105/DUMP_TMC complete in ~50 ms of sim
# time) can land before klippy emits the next periodic Stats line that
# carries the AFEC reading. Without this dwell the `temp=3` assertion
# below misses on ~20-30 % of solo runs - same pattern as
# anycubic_kobra_go (HC32F460) and duet3_6xd (SAME70 external drivers).
G4 P2000
M105

# klippy connected, loaded the dictionary, and built the full config
# against real firmware.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
# DUMP_TMC dumped the first and last TMC2660s - it only completes if the
# firmware round-tripped the 3-byte datagram reads through spidev_transfer.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
# Positive proof the SAM4E AFEC delivered samples: both thermistors read
# ~36 C, so a periodic Stats line carries "temp=3x". A broken AFEC leaves
# them at temp=0.0 with no shutdown.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "temp=3"
# A broken SPI round-trip surfaces as a TMC init failure.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
# A renode-side crash (wrong sysbus peripheral, hook callback error)
# kills serial; klippy then gets EOF and identify / TMC init time out.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
# With the deterministic clock the config / TMC / AFEC path pushes no
# deadline into the firmware's past, so nothing shuts down.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
